Subject: no-sleep mode for the root pass; every load-path allocation checked

30 section 2 patch 3 (S4-02).  The root pass runs at level 7 with the
clock stopped (U1), where nothing may sleep.  dlm_nosleep, which the root
pass sets, makes dlm_zalloc ask KM_NOSLEEP and refuse a request over
1 MiB.  Every allocation on a load path checks for 0, and the load fails
with ENOMEM and leaves the kernel as it was; a module another load holds
is EBUSY instead of a wait.  Outside the mode nothing changes.  The state
harness fails each allocation of a load in turn and checks that nothing
is left behind.

